HST Office: crisp HST icons at the fractional icon scales (150 and 250 %).

Reason: VCL rasterises an SVG icon at its icon scale, which CountDPIScaleFactor rounds to 100,
150, 200 or 250 %. At 150 % (a 144-168 DPI display, 150 and 175 % in the Windows settings) and at
250 % the 1 px lines of the pixel-snapped HST glyphs land between device pixels and turn grey and
blurred. The HST archives now ship every icon also snapped natively for those scales, as
"<name>@150.svg" / "<name>@250.svg" drawn at the final pixel size
(scripts/brand/hst_icon_glyph.py). ImplImageTree::findImage loads that variant at 1.0 when it
exists for the current scale, else the 100 % file as before; themes without variants (Colibre and
the other upstream sets) are unchanged. The disk and memory caches already key rasters by scale.

Applies after hst-icon-theme-hidpi-and-cache.patch.
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme).
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
---
--- a/vcl/inc/HstIconTheme.hxx
+++ b/vcl/inc/HstIconTheme.hxx
@@ -78,6 +78,18 @@
     return OUString();
 }
 
+/// The HST themes ship each SVG icon also pixel-snapped for the fractional icon scales VCL uses
+/// (CountDPIScaleFactor: 150 and 250 %), as "<name>@<percent>.svg" drawn at its final pixel
+/// size. Rasterising the 100 % file at 1.5x would put its 1 px lines between pixels.
+/// Returns the variant's archive path for rPath at nScalePercentage, or empty when none applies.
+inline OUString scaledVariant(std::u16string_view rPath, sal_Int32 nScalePercentage)
+{
+    if ((nScalePercentage != 150 && nScalePercentage != 250) || !o3tl::ends_with(rPath, u".svg"))
+        return OUString();
+    return OUString::Concat(rPath.substr(0, rPath.size() - 4)) + "@"
+           + OUString::number(nScalePercentage) + ".svg";
+}
+
 /// Name of the stamp file inside each "<UserInstallation>/cache/<theme>" directory.
 inline constexpr OUString ICON_CACHE_STAMP_FILE = u"hst-icon-cache-version"_ustr;
 
